🚨 New Publication Alert

@ScienceMagazine Translational Medicine has featured a new study led by Dr. Caroline Geisler, assistant professor at @UK_COP, on a novel brain-targeting approach to obesity treatment.

Current weight loss drugs like GLP-1 receptor agonists (e.g., Ozempic, Wegovy) are highly effective but frequently cause nausea and vomiting. Geisler's team is exploring a new pathway involving the glial peptide ODN, identifying a modified compound (TDN) that suppresses appetite and improves blood sugar control—without gastrointestinal side effects.

This work offers a potential step forward in developing next-generation therapies for obesity and type 2 diabetes.

